		{"id":"g000000000000002","type":"text","text":"## Terra\n### low / medium\n\nDocs and status\nInventories\nMechanical refactors\nRoutine tests\nBounded CRUD after contract freeze","x":220,"y":2500,"width":330,"height":330,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"g000000000000003","type":"text","text":"## Claude Sonnet\n### medium / high\n\nFrontend flows\nForms and components\nResponsive states\nAccessibility\nBrowser smoke tests","x":620,"y":2500,"width":330,"height":330,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"g000000000000004","type":"text","text":"## Sol\n### high\n### xhigh only where marked\n\nContracts\nMigrations / RLS / RPC\nAPI + transactions\nConcurrency\nSecurity + durable jobs","x":1020,"y":2500,"width":330,"height":330,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"g000000000000005","type":"text","text":"## Claude Opus\n### high, focused review\n\nArchitecture ambiguity\nThreat modeling\nIndependent adversarial review\nPhase/release gates\n\nNot the routine implementer.","x":1420,"y":2500,"width":250,"height":330,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"g000000000000006","type":"text","text":"### Spend rule\n\nOne lead model owns the packet. A support/review model receives only the frozen contract, relevant diff, named risks, and verification evidence. Do not duplicate the implementation. No packet defaults to `max` or `ultra`.","x":220,"y":2960,"width":1450,"height":240,"color":"3"},
